# Build output (also commonly redirected out of the source tree via
# CARGO_TARGET_DIR; see .cargo/config.toml).
/target
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Never commit private key material or captured audio.
#
# There are no negations under this heading, and there used to be two that
# looked like there were. `!*.pub` allowed back in a kind of file this
# repository does not hold: a `.pub` is a recipient's hybrid public key, made
# by whoever is going to be sent a recording, and it belongs where they keep
# their keys. `!assets/**` carried its explanation on the same line, and git
# has no inline comments, so the pattern was the whole line including the
# `#` and it never matched a path. Anything under `assets/` that one of the
# rules below would catch is allowed back in by name, on its own line, when
# there is a file to allow: a negation nothing exercises is a negation nobody
# has tested. See F-204 and `tools/audit/fixtures.py`, which now refuses both
# shapes.
*.key
*.pgp
*.gpg
/secrets/
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
*.ogg

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Bundled third-party installers are fetched at packaging time, not committed.
/packaging/vendor/

# Locally generated release-signing material. NEVER commit any of this. The
# private key and the passphrase that protects it live only on the
# maintainer's machine and in GitHub's encrypted secret store, and only the
# public key and the fingerprint are ever meant to leave this folder. A
# negation cannot reach inside an excluded directory, so nothing below can
# rescue a file from here by accident, which is the point of excluding the
# directory rather than the files in it.
/gpg_secrets/
gpg_secrets/
# Armoured OpenPGP files are ignored by default so a private key can never be
# committed by accident. Each file that legitimately lives here is allowed
# back in by its own name below, and each of those rules is exercised by the
# file it names, so none of them can quietly stop working.
*.asc
!website/assets/veilvoice-signing-key.asc
# A public key that is deliberately NOT this project's, used by
# `check::carried`'s tests to prove a download carrying somebody else's key is
# refused. Its private half was never kept and it signs nothing. Allowed back
# in for the same reason as the two above, and named here rather than added
# with `git add -f` so the next person sees why it is tracked: an -f leaves no
# record, and this rule is exactly the kind that swallows a file silently
# (F-203).
!crates/veilvoice-verify/src/check/testdata/*.asc

# Python bytecode. Importing `assets/generate.py` from a check script -- which
# is a reasonable thing to do -- drops a .pyc next to it. A compiled blob is
# precisely what this repository must not contain: the whole claim about the
# artwork is that it comes from a script you can read.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local development files. These are working notes and editor configuration,
# not part of what anybody downloads, and a public repository is not the place
# for either.
#
# NOTE, because untracking is not deleting: `git rm --cached` stops a file
# being published from now on, but every version already committed stays in the
# repository's history and can still be fetched by anyone who clones it.
# Removing it from history means rewriting published history and force-pushing,
# which is a separate and deliberate act. The public-facing replacement for the
# handover notes is ROADMAP.md, which is written to be read by anybody.
HANDOFF.md
HANDOVER.md
.claude/
.claude*/
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md
.mcp.json
.cursor/
.aider*
.vscode/
.idea/

# Agent skills. Installed locally for Rust and security review practice; they
# are tooling for whoever is working on this, not part of what anybody
# downloads, and several carry their own upstream licences.
.claude/skills/
skills/

# The next-session prompt, beside HANDOFF.md. Working notes, not a deliverable.
NEXT-SESSION.md

# Self-signed code-signing material. The private key must never be committed;
# only the public certificate and its fingerprint are published, on the website.
veilvoice-code-key.pem
*.p7s
APPMANIFEST.json.sig

# The dependency watch: the recorded graph, the journal of every version change
# with its date and changelog, the backups and the diffs. Deliberately not
# committed: this directory is a local working record of what the dependencies
# are doing, not something the repository publishes.
#
# Dependabot itself is configured and committed, at `.github/dependabot.yml`.
# This directory is the local half: the same manifests read on demand, with a
# record kept beside them. Nothing in here is read by GitHub.
.dependabot/
